        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=7$.",
          "worked": "At the intersection, the $y$-values are equal.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\log_2(2x-6)&=3\\\\2x-6&=2^3\\\\2x-6&=8\\\\2x&=14\\\\x&=7\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe argument is $2(7)-6=8>0$, so $x=7$ is valid.",
